\tag{fdip}
\title{Staggered fields as exact reductions}
\date{2026-11-23}

\p{The Pauli realization has #{2^n} spin components at each
site. At trivial links its kernel dimension depends on how many
periods are even (\ref{fdip-009Q}). The staggered reduction in
\ref{fdip-009X} chooses a spin line at each site. On which periodic
grids do the ordered spin frames separate the components,
and which operator acts on each one?}

\p{A second question comes from [based cochains](fdip-00SH).
A cell carries its own component, even when several cells have
the same base vertex. On a grid with doubled periods, can the
cell coefficients be arranged as a single staggered field?
The spin reduction allows arbitrary unitary links. The cochain
comparison uses a constant Hermitian fiber and trivial links.}
